toml++: report malformed values that reach parse_value()'s assertions instead of assuming they can't happen

Each hunk pair replaces a TOML_ASSERT_ASSUME in parse_value() that malformed input can break. Debug
builds abort on the assert(); NDEBUG builds turn it into __builtin_assume(), which is undefined
behaviour. With the patch, toml::parse throws toml::parse_error (or returns a failed parse_result
without exceptions), as it does for any other malformed input.

1. TaskSmack #1388: parse_value() opened with TOML_ASSERT_ASSUME(!is_value_terminator(*cp)), but
   the cursor can sit on a terminator there: the '}' in 'm=[}' (an array closed with the wrong
   bracket). This raises the parser's normal error instead, with the same message the key-value
   path already uses ("expected value, saw '}'").

2. TaskSmack #1659: parse_value()'s scan() lambda asserted the same thing on entry. A date
   followed by a space and a digit ('YYYY-MM-DD 1', possibly a space-separated date-time) re-runs
   scan() one character past that digit, which can be a terminator: the second ' ' in
   'h=2000-02-1a 1 1', the newline in 'h=2000-02-01 1\n', the ']' in 'h=[2000-02-01 1]'. scan()
   now returns without scanning, as it already did at end-of-file, so the caller backs up to the
   10-character date and parses only that. The date parser rejects '2000-02-1a', and a valid date
   leaves ' 1 ...' behind, which the key-value and array paths reject.

Base: marzer/tomlplusplus 1e8829b793b66ad17011732a146b8077d379b011 (the GIT_TAG in
cmake/Dependencies.cmake). Patches the split headers under include/ (what TaskSmack compiles
against) and the generated single header toml.hpp alike. Applied by FetchContent's PATCH_COMMAND
through cmake/patches/ApplyPatch.cmake, which skips it when it is already applied. Drop this file
once upstream fixes both assertions (still present in upstream master, 1e8829b, as of 2026-10-09).

diff --git a/include/toml++/impl/parser.inl b/include/toml++/impl/parser.inl
--- a/include/toml++/impl/parser.inl
+++ b/include/toml++/impl/parser.inl
@@ -2552,9 +2552,13 @@
 		{
 			return_if_error({});
 			assert_not_eof();
-			TOML_ASSERT_ASSUME(!is_value_terminator(*cp));
 			push_parse_scope("value"sv);
 
+			// a value terminator here (e.g. the '}' in 'a=[}') is malformed input, not a broken precondition:
+			// report it instead of assuming it can't happen (TOML_ASSERT_ASSUME is UB under NDEBUG)
+			if TOML_UNLIKELY(is_value_terminator(*cp))
+				set_error_and_return_default("expected value, saw '"sv, to_sv(*cp), "'"sv);
+
 			const depth_counter_scope depth_counter{ nested_values };
 			if TOML_UNLIKELY(nested_values > max_nested_values)
 				set_error_and_return_default("exceeded maximum nested value depth of "sv,
@@ -2637,9 +2641,10 @@
 				bool eof_while_scanning = false;
 				const auto scan			= [&]() noexcept(!TOML_COMPILER_HAS_EXCEPTIONS)
 				{
-					if (is_eof())
+					// the date-time rescan below can start on a terminator (the second ' ' in 'a=2000-02-01 1 1'):
+					// nothing to scan, so stop instead of assuming it can't happen (UB under NDEBUG)
+					if (is_eof() || is_value_terminator(*cp))
 						return;
-					TOML_ASSERT_ASSUME(!is_value_terminator(*cp));
 
 					do
 					{
